{#
  Phase 3: VRF-Lite.

  targetVRF 'auto' is the whole difference from phase 2. Instead of leaking
  every selected UDN's routes into the default VRF, OVN-Kubernetes advertises
  each network's subnet inside the VRF that corresponds to that network - so
  blue's pod subnet goes out the blue VRF over the blue VLAN and is never
  seen by red or by the default VRF.

  That is what makes it legitimate for blue and red to carry the SAME pod
  subnet ({{ udn_bgp_tenants | map(attribute='udn_subnet') | first }}), which
  phase 2 could not do. It is also what makes the isolation test meaningful:
  a blue pod must reach blue's external endpoint and must NOT reach red's,
  even though both leaf-side networks are one hop away on the same physical
  link.

  Requires OVN-Kubernetes local gateway mode. In shared gateway mode this CR
  is accepted and VRF-Lite does not work.
#}
apiVersion: k8s.ovn.org/v1
kind: RouteAdvertisements
metadata:
  name: udn-vrflite
spec:
  targetVRF: auto
  networkSelectors:
    - networkSelectionType: ClusterUserDefinedNetworks
      clusterUserDefinedNetworkSelector:
        networkSelector:
          matchLabels:
            {{ udn_bgp_cudn_label_key }}: "enabled"
  nodeSelector: {}
  frrConfigurationSelector:
    matchLabels:
      {{ udn_bgp_frr_label_key }}: fabric-vrflite
  advertisements:
    - PodNetwork
